      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright (c) 2006 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "A 73-year-old morbidly obese patient suffered cortical blindness following coronary angiography. Symptoms rapidly resolved and did not recur following a repeated procedure. Hypoventilation due to narcotics with subsequent hypercarbia and blood-brain barrier breaching may be implicated in the pathogenesis of this complication."
      },
